3ImageToVideo","pos":[-620,5420],"size":[400,380],"flags":{},"order":17,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"clip","name":"clip","type":"CLIP","link":272},{"localized_name":"vae","name":"vae","type":"VAE","link":273},{"localized_name":"首帧","name":"first_frame","shape":7,"type":"IMAGE","link":278},{"localized_name":"末帧","name":"last_frame","shape":7,"type":"IMAGE","link":null},{"localized_name":"提示词","name":"prompt","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"prompt"},"link":279},{"localized_name":"宽度","name":"width","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"width"},"link":276},{"localized_name":"高度","name":"height","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"height"},"link":277},{"localized_name":"长度","name":"length","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"length"},"link":275}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"正向","name":"positive","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[270]},{"localized_name":"Latent","name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[271]}],"title":"MiniMax H3 Image to Video (LynnReal 4-step DMD)","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo","cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.33.0"},"widgets_values":["",768,768,124],"widgets_values_named":{"prompt":"","width":768,"height":768,"length":124}},{"id":138,"type":"PrimitiveStringMultiline","pos":[-1490,6520],"size":[370,390],"flags":{},"order":8,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"值","name":"value","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"value"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"字符串","name":"STRING","type":"STRING","links":[279]}],"title":"Input Text (Prompt)","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"PrimitiveStringMultiline","cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.33.0"},"widgets_values":["Editorial tech product film. The transparent gaming mouse from <Picture 1> in its original scene: a pitch-black studio void with a dark, subtle reflective surface, lit by dramatic duotone vibrant blue and warm neon orange rim lighting, deep soft shadow falloff into pure black. Monochromatic dark palette with electric blue and amber accents. Material motif: glowing internal metallic micro-components and glossy acrylic refractions. The environment is constant throughout.\nSHOT 1: The scene opens exactly on image 1, the mouse resting confidently on the dark surface; the blue and orange lights slowly pulse brighter, refracting deeply through the transparent acrylic shell as the camera executes a slow, deliberate push-in to reveal the intricate circuitry.\nSHOT 2: Cut to an extreme macro profile of the ridged scroll wheel and layered internal micro-components; the camera glides slowly along the side as a sharp beam of warm orange light sweeps across the metallic textures, contrasting perfectly against the deep blue ambient glow.\nSHOT 3: Cut to a low-angle beauty shot: the mouse levitates weightlessly a few centimeters above the dark reflective surface, rotating in a slow, precise orbit; the duotone lighting flares gently along the glassy transparent edges before fading slowly into a sleek silhouette.\nAudio: deep pulsing sub-bass room tone, sharp tactile mechanical clicks, a sweeping glassy whoosh on cuts, and a rising electronic swell that resolves to near-silence on the final fade. "],"widgets_values_named":{"value":"Editorial tech product film. The transparent gaming mouse from <Picture 1> in its original scene: a pitch-black studio void with a dark, subtle reflective surface, lit by dramatic duotone vibrant blue and warm neon orange rim lighting, deep soft shadow falloff into pure black. Monochromatic dark palette with electric blue and amber accents. Material motif: glowing internal metallic micro-components and glossy acrylic refractions. The environment is constant throughout.\nSHOT 1: The scene opens exactly on image 1, the mouse resting confidently on the dark surface; the blue and orange lights slowly pulse brighter, refracting deeply through the transparent acrylic shell as the camera executes a slow, deliberate push-in to reveal the intricate circuitry.\nSHOT 2: Cut to an extreme macro profile of the ridged scroll wheel and layered internal micro-components; the camera glides slowly along the side as a sharp beam of warm orange light sweeps across the metallic textures, contrasting perfectly against the deep blue ambient glow.\nSHOT 3: Cut to a low-angle beauty shot: the mouse levitates weightlessly a few centimeters above the dark reflective surface, rotating in a slow, precise orbit; the duotone lighting flares gently along the glassy transparent edges before fading slowly into a sleek silhouette.\nAudio: deep pulsing sub-bass room tone, sharp tactile mechanical clicks, a sweeping glassy whoosh on cuts, and a rising electronic swell that resolves to near-silence on the final fade. "},"color":"#322","bgcolor":"#533"},{"id":140,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1880,6070],"size":[300,520],"flags":{},"order":9,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Note: Size Settings Reference","properties":{},"widgets_values":["| megapixels | Aspect | Output (multiple=32) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.2 | 16:9 | 608 x 352 |\n| 0.3 | 16:9 | 736 x 416 |\n| 0.4 | 16:9 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.5 | 16:9 | 960 x 544 |\n| 0.6 | 16:9 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.7 | 16:9 | 1152 x 640 |\n| 0.8 | 16:9 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 0.9 | 16:9 | 1280 x 736 |\n| 0.98 | 16:9 | 1344 x 768 (official 768p) |"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"| megapixels | Aspect | Output (multiple=32) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.2 | 16:9 | 608 x 352 |\n| 0.3 | 16:9 | 736 x 416 |\n| 0.4 | 16:9 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.5 | 16:9 | 960 x 544 |\n| 0.6 | 16:9 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.7 | 16:9 | 1152 x 640 |\n| 0.8 | 16:9 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 0.9 | 16:9 | 1280 x 736 |\n| 0.98 | 16:9 | 1344 x 768 (official 768p) |"},"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":200,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-2500,5700],"size":[440,961],"flags":{},"order":10,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Note: LynnReal Standard 4-step DMD","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## LynnReal Standard · 4-step DMD (i2v)\n\nBuilt from the verified r2v graph with the conditioning node swapped.\n\n- `UNETLoader`: `lynnreal_omni_standard_bf16.safetensors`\n- `BasicScheduler`: `simple`, **4 steps**, denoise 1\n- `KSamplerSelect`: `euler`\n- `MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo with `first_frame` from LoadImage`\n- `ResolutionSelector`: 0.98 MP (1344x768), matching the reference script default\n\n**Precision — INT8 (optional)**\n\nThe **`Use INT8 model?`** switch above the loader (default **off**) swaps `UNETLoader` from\n`lynnreal_omni_standard_bf16.safetensors` to `lynnreal_omni_standard_int8.safetensors`. Same\nW8A8 contract as the release's `--precision int8` path: per-output-channel weight scales,\nper-token activation scales, INT32 accumulate; block 0, the last block, the token refiner,\nadaLN and the IO projections stay BF16.\n\n- warm runs are ~8 s faster (41.4 GiB resident instead of 61.7 GiB, so the DiT, the text\n  encoder and both VAEs fit at once), and the file is 44.5 GB on disk instead of 66.3 GB;\n- it is **not the same sample**: quantization shifts the sampling trajectory, so a fixed seed\n  gives a different composition (measured against bf16 at the same seed: 14.8 dB PSNR). Both\n  are the same style and quality; keep the switch off when you want seed-to-seed comparison;\n- the unselected branch is lazy, so leaving the switch off costs nothing.\n"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## LynnReal Standard · 4-step DMD (i2v)\n\nBuilt from the verified r2v graph with the conditioning node swapped.\n\n- `UNETLoader`: `lynnreal_omni_standard_bf16.safetensors`\n- `BasicScheduler`: `simple`, **4 steps**, denoise 1\n- `KSamplerSelect`: `euler`\n- `MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo with `first_frame` from LoadImage`\n- `ResolutionSelector`: 0.98 MP (1344x768), matching the reference script default\n\n**Precision — INT8 (optional)**\n\nThe **`Use INT8 model?`** switch above the loader (default **off**) swaps `UNETLoader` from\n`lynnreal_omni_standard_bf16.safetensors` to `lynnreal_omni_standard_int8.safetensors`. Same\nW8A8 contract as the release's `--precision int8` path: per-output-channel weight scales,\nper-token activation scales, INT32 accumulate; block 0, the last block, the token refiner,\nadaLN and the IO projections stay BF16.\n\n- warm runs are ~8 s faster (41.4 GiB resident instead of 61.7 GiB, so the DiT, the text\n  encoder and both VAEs fit at once), and the file is 44.5 GB on disk instead of 66.3 GB;\n- it is **not the same sample**: quantization shifts the sampling trajectory, so a fixed seed\n  gives a different composition (measured against bf16 at the same seed: 14.8 dB PSNR). Both\n  are the same style and quality; keep the switch off when you want seed-to-seed comparison;\n- the unselected branch is lazy, so leaving the switch off costs nothing.\n"},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":203,"type":"ComfySwitchNode","pos":[-790,5040],"size":[240,80],"flags":{},"order":16,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"为假时","name":"on_false","shape":7,"type":"MODEL","link":293},{"localized_name":"为真时","name":"on_true","shape":7,"type":"MODEL","link":294},{"localized_name":"切换","name":"switch","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"switch"},"link":295}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"输出","name":"output","type":"MODEL","links":[252,292]}],"title":"Model: bf16 (off) / INT8 (on)","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"ComfySwitchNode"},"widgets_values":[false],"widgets_values_named":{"switch":false}},{"id":202,"type":"PrimitiveBoolean","pos":[-592.422326565208,6298.839809238929],"size":[313.569921875,60],"flags":{},"order":11,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"值","name":"value","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"value"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"布尔","name":"BOOLEAN","type":"BOOLEAN","links":[295]}],"title":"Use INT8 model?  (off = bf16, the default)","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"PrimitiveBoolean"},"widgets_values":[false],"widgets_values_named":{"value":false}},{"id":137,"type":"LoadImage","pos":[-1011.1456309494123,6138.092233553084],"size":[290,330],"flags":{},"order":12,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"图像","name":"image","type":"COMBO","widget":